<Base title="Research">
  <p class="eyebrow">Research / Direction</p><h1>Research principles</h1>
  <p class="lead">Study infrastructure products and their security boundaries, automate repeatable research tasks with AI, and advance methods through human understanding and independently verified evidence.</p>
  <div class="grid">
    <section class="panel"><h3>Infrastructure</h3><p>Study the architecture and internals of infrastructure software, including operating systems, network services, virtualization, containers and cloud systems, through reproducible local experiments.</p></section>
    <section class="panel"><h3>Discovery</h3><p>Study prior research and known vulnerabilities, then investigate authorized open-source and commercial infrastructure products. Prefer validated existing tools where appropriate.</p></section>
    <section class="panel"><h3>Validation</h3><p>Separate observations from claims, reproduce findings, document scope and limitations, and seek independent validation.</p></section>
  </div>
  <h2>Research methodology</h2>
  <p>AI executes. Humans understand, verify, and advance.</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Understand infrastructure:</strong> Study architecture, internal mechanisms and security boundaries.</li>
    <li><strong>Research and engineering:</strong> Use AI agents and validated tools to automate repeatable research, development and experiments within approved scope.</li>
    <li><strong>Independent verification:</strong> Reproduce observations, preserve evidence, test assumptions and record limitations.</li>
    <li><strong>Human technical understanding:</strong> Document principles, evidence and technical decisions in individual blogs, in publishable form.</li>
    <li><strong>Continuous improvement:</strong> Use verified findings to improve research tools, designs and methods.</li>
    <li><strong>External validation:</strong> Seek coordinated disclosure, eligible bug bounties, CVEs and accepted upstream security contributions where appropriate.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Humans remain responsible for research scope, technical decisions, validation and disclosure. Automation is a research direction, not a claim of proven autonomous discovery performance.</p>
  <h2>Infrastructure map</h2><p>A public study resource for the infrastructure track: 16 infrastructure areas linked to open-source software, known exploited vulnerabilities (CISA KEV), security incidents and company services, updated daily from KEV. Korean only for now.</p>
  <div class="actions" style="margin-top:12px"><a class="button primary" href="/ko/research/infra-map/">Open the map (Korean)</a></div>
  <h2>What counts as a result?</h2><p>We distinguish educational reproductions and technical notes from original vulnerability discoveries, accepted security contributions and externally validated outcomes. We do not claim a CVE, bounty or upstream acceptance before it is confirmed.</p>
  <h2>Responsible disclosure</h2><p>Test only authorized targets. Coordinate with maintainers before publishing sensitive vulnerability details. Do not publish private credentials or embargoed artifacts.</p>
</Base>
